1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,160
The dunes in this game sparkle as you move.

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,740
Even grains smaller than a pixel

3
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:08,040
do not all need individual 3D geometry.

4
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:12,540
The developers separated rough grain, tiny glints,

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,920
and broad highlights.

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,160
Look separately at the small bright points

7
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:17,680
and the broad light across a dune.

8
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,720
The tiny points suggest grains;

9
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,840
the broad light reveals the dune’s shape.

10
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:24,940
First, small patterns describe

11
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,640
which way the sand surface faces.

12
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,880
That direction is called a normal.

13
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:30,920
But in smaller textures used at a distance,

14
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:32,880
those directional differences blur together.

15
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:37,700
The team adjusted the distribution of directions to retain grain in smaller textures.

16
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:39,260
Imagine many tiny mirrors

17
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,120
tilted in different directions.

18
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,260
Under the same light,

19
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:45,400
only some faces send light toward us.

20
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,680
The pattern stores those direction differences

21
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,440
instead of modeling every grain.

22
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,340
Tiny glints are added on top.

23
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:53,840
Apply sharp highlights to small grain,

24
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:55,780
and a still image can look convincing.

25
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:57,420
But when the camera moves,

26
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:00,440
bright points may flicker unstably.

27
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:03,460
Intended sparkle and unstable flickering are different.

28
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:05,380
Here the camera moves

29
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:07,520
while the dune stays in place.

30
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:10,240
Yet the small bright points change.

31
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:11,680
The sand is not covered in tiny lamps;

32
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:15,160
its reflections change with the view.

33
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:18,000
The first calculation considered both light and view.

34
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,220
The replacement examined how much a small surface

35
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:22,280
faces the camera.

36
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:24,560
This adjusts the tiny lights revealed

37
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,000
as the camera moves.

38
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,200
This is an artistic rendering choice,

39
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:31,100
rather than an exact model of real sand.

40
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,780
As the view moves in this comparison model,

41
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:34,820
different small faces become bright.

42
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:36,860
The goal is not simply more bright dots,

43
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:39,320
but sand that remains convincing in motion.

44
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,920
Near the edge of a sand dune,

45
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,460
when we see the surface obliquely,

46
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:45,040
the pattern can stretch and spread.

47
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,080
A mask identifies these regions

48
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:49,300
and reduces the glint effect there.

49
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:51,700
Instead of applying it strongly everywhere,

50
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,860
the problematic regions are handled separately.

51
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,340
Compare looking down onto the dune

52
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:57,680
with viewing it at a grazing angle.

53
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:00,080
Emphasizing stretched highlights equally

54
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:02,160
would spoil the tiny-grain appearance.

55
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:05,320
Finally, broad light flows over the dunes.

56
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,920
This reflection reveals their large shapes.

57
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,560
Three treatments of light come together to complete the sand.

58
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,740
Tiny bright points alone

59
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:14,380
would not clearly describe the dune’s rounded shape.

60
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:15,980
Read the coarse texture, fine sparkles,

61
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,000
and broad reflection together.
